# 032 · Checks before a rig is deployed

**Status:** `PROPOSED` · **Version:** [v0.4.0](../roadmap.md#v040)

## What

A server-side dry run of a rig's manifests, before every deploy, that reports Pod Security levels, quota and admission webhooks in plain words. A warning before the judge gets a GPU that the cluster shares (time-slicing or MIG).

## Why

A deploy should fail before it starts, not halfway. Judge timing needs a GPU of its own.

## Done when

- [ ] Both checks run before each deploy, with tests on a local cluster.

## Decisions

None yet.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the roadmap.

